WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.643
Today there are no letters. Today is about the body, the pencil, and the paper.

2
00:00:05.093 --> 00:00:11.905
Watch first. The first one on the page is done for you: show it, do the next one together, and your child does the rest.

3
00:00:12.405 --> 00:00:14.984
Watch first. Then do the same with your child.

4
00:00:15.484 --> 00:00:19.008
When writing is tiring, it is often one of these three things.

5
00:00:19.458 --> 00:00:25.919
One. Sit. Feet flat on the floor, or on a box. Bottom back in the chair. Both arms on the table.

6
00:00:26.369 --> 00:00:31.234
Two. Pinch. Thumb and pointer finger pinch the pencil, just above the cut wood.

7
00:00:31.684 --> 00:00:35.296
The pencil rests on the tall finger. The last two fingers tuck in.

8
00:00:35.746 --> 00:00:39.734
The picture on the page shows the three places, with a number on each.

9
00:00:40.184 --> 00:00:45.984
If your child holds the pencil another way, and writing is easy and you can read it, leave it alone.

10
00:00:46.584 --> 00:00:53.347
Three. Paper. Lean it a little. For a right hand, the top leans left. For a left hand, the top leans right.

11
00:00:53.797 --> 00:00:57.351
The other hand is the helper hand. It holds the paper still.

12
00:00:57.801 --> 00:01:02.970
A left-handed child pinches a little higher up the pencil, to see the letters as they come.

13
00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:07.758
Do the three together, and let your child mark each box. Then step away.

14
00:01:08.208 --> 00:01:16.007
Job two is five moves: a tall line, a short line, a bounce, a round one, and a slant. Every letter is made of these.

15
00:01:16.457 --> 00:01:23.586
Each gray move has a green dot. Your child starts there, traces six, makes more, and circles their own best one.

16
00:01:24.036 --> 00:01:28.055
At the end, your child shows you how they sit, their pinch, and their paper.
